WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:05.840
Hello?

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.800
Hello?

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.720
Hello?

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.000
Hey, can you hear me?

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.120
Daisy?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.480
-Hey.
-Oh, hello.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:16.840
It's been
a long time, right?

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.240
I know.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.280
I literally haven't seen you
for ten years.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.320
-One of them, innit.
-That's mad.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.880
I remember that era
being so special to me.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:26.960
We were just kids

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.280
from a little rinky-dink
home town.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.880
I find it so bizarre
that we found each other.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:31.760
I know.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.000
I just think our year was
so different to other years.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.760
We were
the gayest year ever.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.480
This is weird.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.440
Wow,
it still smells the same.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.840
Over by the fishies!

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.440
This is so cute.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.520
There he is!

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.160
Plié!

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.920
Over and out, bitches.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.080
-Oh, well, hello.
-Hello.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.440
You are my pot of gold.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.800
Honest to God…

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:01.840
Hey!

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.080
I'm sorry, but I wouldn't
put this on the wall.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.360
Josh!

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.480
Josh!

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.440
What?

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.880
Pull yourself together!

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.040
Me and my daughter.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.480
Last day of school!

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:16.440
Say something
about the snow.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.320
It's snowing!

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.080
When was
the last time you were here?

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.320
It would have been
the last year of sixth form.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.200
Kathleen!

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.960
Being on school grounds

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.360
and walking around now,
it's just like… yeah.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.880
It's so… It's…
Yeah. It's really weird.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.960
Did you have
lessons in here?

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.440
I think when I was
in Year 7.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.320
I sat over there.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.720
Do you remember doing
this self-portrait?

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.680
-I hated it.
-Same.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.840
I drew Reese Witherspoon.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.720
No one taught us
how to do the colour right,

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:42.600
by the way.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.160
-What brown?
-Yeah.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.040
-Anyway, here's your seat.
-Thank you.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.640
I'll sit behind the camera.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.680
Just gonna move forward.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.520
We're gonna start
with an icebreaker,

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.280
-which is…
-A role play?

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.160
Try and name
as many queer people

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.240
in our year as possible.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.960
Are we including
the bi people as well?

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.040
-Yes.
-Well, you.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.800
-Me.
-Kathleen.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:04.800
-Owen.
-Josh.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.360
-Lauren.
-Ellie Kelly.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.880
-Kevert.
-Callum Davis.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.880
-Louise.
-Scott came out, didn't he?

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.440
Connor Wanklin.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.040
Hannah Williams?

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.640
When I started doing drag,
some people were just like…

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.440
You'd be surprised.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.920
I'm sure I'm missing
a good few people.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.760
Oh, my God, there's,
like, all these names.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.640
There's loads and they've
all gone out of my head.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.240
You beat Kath.
Kath got about six.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.680
You can just name
our friend group.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.760
This is what happens
when you come to Tewkesbury.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.640
You go gay
and you get filmed.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.760
At the time, in school,
it didn't seem strange

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.560
that there were
so many queer people

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:39.640
in our year group.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.920
It just seemed
very, very normal.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.120
Gays in the house!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.960
And it's only really
looking back, realising,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.280
actually, that was
really special because

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.240
to have over 30 people
in one year group

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:52.320
identifying somewhere
on the spectrum

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.480
in this tiny town
in 2005 to 2012,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.240
not the same
in the year above,

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.440
not the same
in the year below,

00:02:58.520 --> 00:02:59.800
I don't know
how it happened,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.160
but I'm just
so glad that it did.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.040
We call Tewkesbury
Twinkleberry,

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.120
or Twink for short.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.800
Good old Tewkesbury.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.560
It's a really
picturesque town,

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.720
like the gorgeous old abbey.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.440
It's like a small town
in every sense of the word.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.600
There's always
a mutual friend

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.360
that will know who you are.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.800
You generally can't
walk down the street

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.040
without someone being like,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.120
"How's your mum doing?"

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.280
or, "How's
your grandad doing?"

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.160
You're like,

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.120
"I just wanna go
and get some bread."

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.280
It's like…
It's one of those.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.760
I would say Tewkesbury is
a very white town as well.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.760
Being a mixed-race kid
in this town,

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.600
I remember
that I stood out a lot.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.560
You constantly felt like
you were being watched,

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.760
so for me, it was just like
I had to have a clean break.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.400
I come home
just to see family,

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.960
and on the odd occasion,
to see friends, but…

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.000
that is such a small pool

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.400
cos I never really felt
at home in Tewkesbury.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.680
I feel like
there is a dark side.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.320
Yeah.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.400
I'd say it's a thing about
any small English town.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.880
There's always undercurrents
of people's secrets.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.920
I don't know. I feel like
I'm talking ill of it,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.800
but I love
Tewkesbury to bits

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.600
'cause it's where I'm from
and it's where I grew up,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.840
and I had a great time.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.280
Do you feel like
a bit conflicted

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.360
when speaking
about Tewkesbury?

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.600
You don't want
to bad-mouth it,

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.800
but you should
be able to say

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.800
there's bits about where you
grew up that you don't like.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.680
It's just Tewkesbury,
isn't it?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:34.960
I always felt like

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.640
if I had a good day
in school and stuff, like,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.200
then home would be OK.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.520
I knew at an early age
that I was gay,

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.280
and for me, I was having
to hold that in.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.360
-Hey, kids.
-Hey!

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.000
My first step was
just telling my friends

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:48.480
because if I could
open up with them,

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.040
then hopefully then in time,

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.200
I could do the same
with my family.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.600
We'd just had PE,

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.440
and I remember
telling some friends.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.040
And it was meant to stay
between those guys,

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.120
but obviously our year group
being our year group,

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.520
everyone found out
really quickly,

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.520
and also being in
that small, confined space,

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.480
everyone just, like,
found out,

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.440
and I don't know,
it was weird

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.280
because I'm just expecting
hate to have flooded over,

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:15.360
but everyone was like,

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.760
"Oh, my God!
Do you know she's gay?"

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:17.840
And it was just, like…

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.360
Everyone was just kinda
happy about it.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.080
And I was just like,
"What's going on?"

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.080
And then like the next week,
someone else had come out,

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.720
and then it was just, like,
this chain of people then.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:30.160
I think I was probably
13-14 when I came out.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.120
Look at him!

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.920
I remember growing up
and, like, buying

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.320
the Baby Spice doll
and I was like,

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.720
"No, I need
to have all five girls."

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.000
My mum,

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.920
she went all the way
to Toys "R" Us,

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.920
bought me all five girls,

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.520
and I think
she knew by then.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:46.960
She was like,
"Yeah, he's gay."

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.000
I think it was
fairly obvious

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.120
with the friend group
we hung out with

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:51.920
that I was gay.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:53.600
Hi, Mum!

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.600
People stopped asking
because any time they did,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.960
they would then get attacked
by my friends

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.160
or it'd be like,
"Oh, what of it?"

00:05:58.720 --> 00:05:59.520
And then,

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:00.680
there was
this one girl at school

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.240
that was basically
a known gossip,

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.840
and I thought, "I'm happy
for everyone to know."

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.240
Told her,

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.680
it then spread out
to the wider world.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.400
I came back in Year 12
and someone asked me once.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:12.320
"Are you gay?
I heard you came out."

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.040
I was like, "Yeah."
And she was like, "Ah."

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:15.720
And that was that,
and then, no one…

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.880
no one then said
anything about it again.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.520
I didn't come out.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.680
I think
I really resented the fact

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.040
that other people
had to be part of…

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.120
this experience of mine.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.040
Girl, you so fine!

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.000
I also just like spoke
about liking girls

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.160
with my friends,

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.760
and that was it.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.760
-Hey, beautiful!
-Hey.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.240
I think there was

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:37.840
the first two or three
people who came out,

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:38.920
and then after that,

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.320
I don't think people really
came out to the year.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.280
For the large part,

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.680
there didn't seem to be
a lot of judgment.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.320
Do your thang!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.000
Up until Year 9,

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:52.120
I was this, like,
very scared person.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.560
I do remember
doing a paper round

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.200
and literally thinking
in my mind, I was like,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:57.880
"Please don't be gay.
Like, I can't be gay."

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.360
In school, I was
two years below you guys.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.720
There was only one
other gay guy in my year,

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:04.960
but…

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.600
I don't know, I just felt
more at home with you guys.

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:10.240
Less people would come up
and have something to say

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.240
'cause you had
a group of people

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.080
who were open and proud

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.240
and would fight
the fight with you.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:22.200
So, I'd spend every moment
I could with you guys.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:26.240
I just have one thing
for you to read.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:27.120
Yep.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.520
This is a letter
that we wrote to the MP.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.400
I was 16,
so you would have been 14.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.760
-Did we write it together?
-Yeah. At Ed's house.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.520
It was me, you, Josh, Kath…

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.400
Yeah.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:38.920
Harv and a couple of others.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.520
Could you please
read it out to the room?

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.040
Blah-blah… Oh,
these are long sentences!

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.000
Here I am calling for gay
marriage to be legalised.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.920
We find it
absolutely disgusting

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.040
that even in 2012…

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.360
…heterosexual people
have privileges

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.280
that homosexual and bisexual
people do not have.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.240
If you were denied the right
to marry a woman,

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.560
based on something
as irrelevant

00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.640
as her race or height…

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.080
…I'm sure you'll feel
discriminated against

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.520
and want to alter the law.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.800
Please try and see the world

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.320
through another
person's eyes.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.960
You're after all
trying to lead

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.360
the people of our town.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:13.440
Wow, that's crazy.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.280
2012. It's not even
long ago, is it?

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.000
-So, that was to the MP.
-OK.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.600
And this was from the MP.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.640
Oh! This I have not seen.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.520
Yeah, I don't think
I did share it with anyone.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:24.720
It's probably
not worth sharing,

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.080
but let's give it a read.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:28.520
Thank you for your recent
email about an article

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.600
which appeared
in local press

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.880
with regards
to same-sex marriage.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.240
I will have
to disappoint you

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.680
by saying that I believe
that marriage

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.120
is between a man
and a woman.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.040
I do not discriminate
against people

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.600
because of their sexuality.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.120
Indeed, I have friends,

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.720
one of which is
a very senior MP,

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.000
who are homosexuals.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.520
And, as an aside,

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.440
I have friends
from other continents

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:49.880
such as Africa.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.040
I abhor discrimination

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.480
and believe that prejudice
is born of ignorance.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.760
I have nothing against
couples of the same sex

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:57.840
having relationships…

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.600
…or even cohabiting…

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.960
…but I do not believe
that they can be married.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:06.000
With best wishes,
Laurence Robertson MP.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.920
As a queer person,
I think you just

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.360
grow up expecting people,

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.560
to a certain extent,
to be homophobic.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:23.120
Also you remember just
that kind of feeling that

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.720
other people were starting
to hate on me,

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.200
which wasn't
a feeling I had before.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:29.520
So… was it me or was it
because I was gay?

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.400
I was very reclusive

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:35.360
because I was just
always terrified of people.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.280
It was a constant fear that,
if I went out,

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.840
what could happen to me?

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:42.320
People would push me over,
I got spat on.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.840
I got tied to a tree…

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:46.880
and thrown rocks at.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:50.040
Um, I got pinned down

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:53.240
and someone snotted
a bogey in my face.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.040
I used to always
put myself down

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.680
and, um, just make
myself feel like shit…

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:04.520
because I was just so camp
and I just felt like

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:06.040
the other boys
just didn't get it.

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:08.800
And I just remember feeling
really uncomfortable…

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:11.200
with myself, but then,
I guess, growing up,

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.280
I felt like I wasn't
on my own.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:14.640
It's in the windows!

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.800
I just didn't
give a shit anymore.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.760
And I still don't, you know?

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:20.920
So, yeah.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:23.800
I felt that you guys did
look after me.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.840
In a way
that my parents couldn't.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.920
I think if they knew
to the extent,

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.880
well, they would have
wanted to help more,

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.000
but they couldn't.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.640
So, I found a family,
within school,

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:38.320
of people that were like me.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:46.440
As a year group,
everyone always

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.720
used to look out
for each other.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:50.200
You were like kind
of protected in a way

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.840
'cause you had these people
that were like

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.280
that barrier between you
and that hate.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.080
You don't need
to feel alone in it.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.200
There's a group of people
that you can connect with,

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.240
somewhere,
maybe two years above.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.760
Even in a tiny little town
like Twinkleberry.

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:19.920
I feel so lucky
to have always had

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.240
queer people around me

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:25.480
who were fairly happy
to explore their sexuality

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.600
at a time and in a place

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.200
where that wasn't
encouraged.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.320
I don't think I've ever

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:31.840
gotten closer
to other people

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:33.760
than the friends
we've had here.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:34.840
The funny thing is

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:37.640
I still have more gay
friends from this tiny town

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:40.080
than I do from living
in the centre of Birmingham

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.560
where there's
a massive gay scene.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.040
It's so bizarre.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:47.360
The funniest part

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.600
is that we're literally
all walking around

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:51.360
calling this town Twink.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.080
I don't know whether people

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.480
don't know the gay meaning
of that word.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:58.600
Twink! Like who…

00:11:58.680 --> 00:11:59.800
It's full of twinks!

